msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/workflow.md:147
msgid "`validate` misses cycles of three or more nodes when some node has no incoming edge; the native runtime rejects them on submission."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/workflow.md:149
msgid "A `Recv`, `Lock` or `Send` that can run before its partner may block forever on the native runtime. Order such nodes with edges."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/workflow.md:151
msgid "A `Signal` wakes only a `Wait` that is already blocked. Do not join them by an edge: `Wait -> Signal` deadlocks, because the `Wait` completes only after the `Signal` ran, and `Signal -> Wait` loses the signal. Make the `Wait` ready first instead, for example by putting another node in front of the `Signal`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/workflow.md:156
msgid "A single `Barrier` node in a group fails at run time with status `14`; a barrier needs at least two nodes at the same depth. Use one barrier capability per group: two groups at different depths that share a capability share its arrival counter, and the native runtime can then hang."
msgstr ""

